# PyPI package (`pip install krepis`) — NOT nousergon-lib (git-tag-pinned
# below); the two are unrelated packages. Floor matches the pin
# alpha-engine-config uses for the same module (currently on PyPI at 0.10.2).
#
# [openai] extra (I2997): live/morning_brief.py's Phase-2 morning-brief
# consumer (config#664 / L4574) now builds its rerun-driven, four-gate-
# throttled brief via krepis.llm.LLMClient's OpenRouter transport
# (DeepSeek V4 Flash) instead of a raw anthropic.Anthropic() client — the
# fleet-wide "off direct Anthropic API" migration (EvalJudge Batches is the
# sole deliberate exception, per Brian's 2026-07-19 ruling). The extra pulls
# `openai` (OpenAI-compatible SDK, used against OpenRouter's base_url). Key
# resolution moved from the (verified-dead-in-production, no secrets.toml on
# this box) st.secrets path to nousergon_lib.secrets.get_secret
# ("OPENROUTER_API_KEY") — SSM-first via the box's existing
# alpha-engine-ssm-read policy, no new IAM. v0.12.2 is the earliest tag
# carrying the OpenRouter unresolved/leaked-tool-call safety fix in
# krepis.llm; the >=0.14.0 floor here already clears that.
# Floor raised to 0.18.8 (2026-07-27): the weekly SF's spot boxes build THIS
# repo's venv and run `python -m krepis.ssm_log_capture run --correlation-id ...`.
# That flag does not exist before 0.18.8, and 0.18.8 is also where the
# correlation id became MANDATORY — both halves of one contract. The compiled
# lockfile was resolving to 0.18.0, which argparse-failed every SSM stage on a
# freshly-built box ("the following arguments are required: --slug, --log",
# because the unknown --correlation-id swallowed --slug as its value).
#
# This only surfaced once nousergon-data#975 moved weekly dispatch onto a
# per-execution spot box that builds this venv from scratch; the long-lived
# dashboard box had 0.18.8 installed out-of-band, masking the stale pin.
# Floor raised to 0.59.3 (2026-08-13, alpha-engine-config-I7260): peak-RSS
# measurement lives in `krepis.ssm_dispatcher`, which is the chokepoint every
# weekly-SF spot step runs through — and THIS venv is the interpreter that runs
# it, whatever the dispatcher repos pin for themselves. Measured on the box
# 2026-08-13: `alpha-engine-dashboard/.venv` had krepis 0.54.0 installed, so
# without this bump the stage RAM budget publishes nothing and every stage
# renders UNOBSERVED. No dependency set changed between 0.54.0 and 0.59.x
# (`git diff v0.54.0 origin/main -- pyproject.toml` touches the version line
# only), so this is a pin move, not a resolution change.
# Floor raised again to 0.59.6 (2026-08-14, alpha-engine-config-I7372): the
# spot-bootstrap collapse — infrastructure/spot_backtest.sh and
# infrastructure/spot_train.sh now render their bootstrap via
# `krepis.spot_bootstrap.render_bootstrap`/`.render_install_deps` instead of
# hand-carrying it, and tests/test_spot_bootstrap_cutover.py imports
# `scan_for_inline_bootstraps`. Neither symbol exists in 0.59.3 — measured:
# `pip install krepis==0.59.3; python -c "import krepis.spot_bootstrap as m;
# print(hasattr(m, 'scan_for_inline_bootstraps'))"` prints False;
# `krepis.spot_bootstrap` itself (the whole module) does not exist before
# 0.59.x's EC2-spot/SSM resilience surface, per this file's own package
# summary line.
# Floor raised again to 0.59.14 (2026-08-19, alpha-engine-config-I7609/I7675):
# `krepis.spot_evidence` — the spot-teardown chokepoint that copies a FAILED
# run's S3 staging to `_spot_evidence/` BEFORE deleting it — first ships in
# 0.59.13. THIS venv is the interpreter every weekly-SF spot launcher resolves
# as `LIB_PYTHON` (`nousergon-data/infrastructure/_spot_common.sh:62`), so a pin
# below 0.59.13 means the module is absent on the launcher and the launcher
# takes its fallback branch. Measured live 2026-08-19 on `i-08d7e8358772b280c`
# (DataPhase1 of `watch-rerun-2026-08-18-3`):
# `No module named krepis.spot_evidence` → staging RETAINED, un-lifecycled.
# The same absence on 2026-08-15 let `PredictorBacktest`'s teardown delete the
# only uncapped copy of its own failure output; that cause is permanently
# unrecoverable.
#
# UPPER BOUND `<0.59.15` IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT TIDINESS (alpha-engine-config-I7634).
# 0.59.15 makes `krepis.session_dlp` shell out to a `gitleaks` binary and FAIL
# CLOSED when it is absent. This box has no gitleaks and `deploy-on-merge.sh`
# installs straight from this lockfile, so a bump past 0.59.14 puts the DLP hook
# on a box that cannot satisfy it — and it surfaces as an LLM failure naming a
# scanner, not as a pin problem. Verified by file, not by changelog:
# `git grep -l gitleaks v0.59.14 -- src/krepis/` is empty; the same command at
# v0.59.15 returns `src/krepis/session_dlp.py`.
# REMOVE THIS CAP when I7634 deliverable 1 provisions gitleaks 8.30.1 on this
# box AND adds it to the provisioning the box is rebuilt from. Not before.
